Distribution: Slackware Linux 9.1
Hardware Environment: AMD XP 2200, ATI Radeon Mobility 9000 (see below for lspci
output)
Software Environment: just the console, no X
Problem Description:

Since I upgraded from kernel 2.6.6 to 2.6.7 the font on the console has become
invisible (black on black). I can still see the bright cursor moving around the
screen, and I can login blindly, but I cannot read any output on the console.

When booting the first few lines of output can still be seen, then the letters
turn black. It's booting too fast to see where exactly it becomes black.

I haven't made any kernel configuration changes when I have upgraded the kernel
(used make oldconfig and answered the few new settings with 'n').

There is a vesa error in dmesg, but I use vga=normal in lilo.conf. Maybe this
has something to do with the problem anyway? See further below for the complete
dmesg output.

Steps to reproduce:

I'm only using kernel 2.6.7 on one system (notebook) so far. All I did was to
compile the kernel with the same config and boot it. Font turns black while
booting...

Below are outputs of lspci, dmesg, config.gz and so on...


